            <div class="body-text">
                <p>Keri Selig is an independent producer with her own production company, Intuition Productions, where she is actively producing features and television projects.</p>
                <p>Selig was an executive producer on the remake of the science fiction thriller <span data-field="film_title_1">{{ film_title_1 }}</span> for Paramount Pictures and Scott Rundin Screenplay. She directed the picture and produced the film <span data-field="film_title_2">{{ film_title_2 }}</span> for Paramount Pictures. She also produced the film <span data-field="film_title_3">{{ film_title_3 }}</span> for Paramount Pictures.</p>
                <p>Presently, Selig is in post production on <span data-field="film_title_4">{{ film_title_4 }}</span> and <span data-field="film_title_5">{{ film_title_5 }}</span>. Passengers is a supernatural thriller about a grief-stricken man who finds himself in a strange, isolated town. <span data-field="film_title_6">{{ film_title_6 }}</span> is a drama about a man who is trying to escape his past. <span data-field="film_title_7">{{ film_title_7 }}</span> is a thriller about a man who is trying to escape his past.</p>
                <p>Another Ronnie Christian project that Selig has in development is <span data-field="film_title_8">{{ film_title_8 }}</span>, a supernatural thriller set in a small town. <span data-field="film_title_9">{{ film_title_9 }}</span> is attached to direct and Hugh Whitemore (My House in Umbria, The Gathering Storm) is set to write.</p>
                <p>Another project Selig is currently producing is <span data-field="film_title_10">{{ film_title_10 }}</span> by Dan Gordon (The Hurricane, Murder in the First).</p>
            </div>
        </div>
        <div class="right-column">
            <div class="body-text">
                <p>An original screenplay about the life of <span data-field="subject_name">{{ subject_name }}</span>. This film is being financed by Brightlight Pictures.</p>
                <p>Another project Selig is developing is the feature adaptation of <span data-field="source_material">{{ source_material }}</span>, the graphic novel from Orson Scott Card (Ender's Game) and Oscar-winning special effects artist <span data-field="artist_name">{{ artist_name }}</span>. The film is attached to make his directorial debut on <span data-field="film_title_11">{{ film_title_11 }}</span>. <span data-field="The Swimmer">{{ The Swimmer }}</span> is attached to make his directorial debut on <span data-field="film_title_12">{{ film_title_12 }}</span>. <span data-field="The Swimmer">{{ The Swimmer }}</span> is attached to make his directorial debut on <span data-field="film_title_13">{{ film_title_13 }}</span>.</p>
                <p>In addition, Selig has various television projects in active development including <span data-field="tv_project_1">{{ tv_project_1 }}</span>, <span data-field="tv_project_2">{{ tv_project_2 }}</span>, which is set up at <span data-field="location">{{ location }}</span>, and <span data-field="tv_project_3">{{ tv_project_3 }}</span>. <span data-field="The Swimmer">{{ The Swimmer }}</span> is a modern-day look at adoption, and Rodney Vacca (Three to Tango). Set to shoot in summer 2007.</p>
